# SEO

- Canonical site URL is `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` via `src/lib/seo/site.ts`. No trailing slash.
- `robots.ts` allows `/` and disallows `/studio`, `/login`, `/denied`, `/auth`. Point sitemap at `${SITE_URL}/sitemap.xml`.
- `sitemap.ts` includes static public paths plus published articles, tags, and projects. Never list drafts or studio routes. Do not add `/cv`.
- RSS is `/feed.xml` (latest published articles). Escape XML. Include `xmlns:atom`, `atom:link` self, and `<language>en</language>`. Keep `alternates` on root metadata.
- JSON-LD helpers live in `src/components/seo/json-ld.tsx` (`Person`, `WebSite` + SearchAction, `BlogPosting`, `BreadcrumbList`). Escape `<` in JSON. SearchAction target is `${SITE_URL}/search?q={search_term_string}`.
- OG images: `src/components/seo/og-image.tsx` plus default `src/app/opengraph-image.tsx` and per-route files under articles/projects. Stay 1200×630.
- `/llms.txt` lists the site name, description, and published article/project absolute URLs only. No drafts or studio.
- Studio routes set `robots: { index: false, follow: false }`. Search with a `q` param is `noindex, follow`.
- After new public routes, update sitemap, robots (if needed), and JSON-LD in the same change.

Audit workflow: `seo` skill.
